# DM control tower — manual-first, AI optional

The **Workshop** is the DM's control tower for session prep. The **Virtual Table (VTT)** is the table at play. Both must deliver immense value **without** AI.

## Core principle

- AI is a **feature**, not a requirement. Every workflow must work end-to-end with no API keys.
- AI **accelerates** prep (draft, suggest, generate images) — it must never be the only path to a usable result.
- Prefer **curation, persistence, and reuse** (seeds, parties, sheets, maps, session state) over one-off generation.
- The **Workshop Library** is the canonical repository — categorized assets with SRD vs user-owned provenance (see `workshop-library` rule).

## When building features

**Do**

- Provide manual create, edit, import, and export paths alongside any AI action.
- Design empty states for "add manually" or "import .md", not only "Generate".
- Keep user-owned content in browser storage; bundled rules stay SRD-only (see `/legal`).
- Label AI actions clearly; when keys are missing, the rest of the app stays fully usable.

**Don't**

- Gate core Workshop or VTT tools behind generation or API calls.
- Make AI the default or only way to create parties, sheets, tokens, maps, or session data.
- Remove manual controls when adding AI helpers — add "fast forward", don't replace the tool.

## Zone focus

| Zone | Without AI | AI enhances |
|------|------------|-------------|
| **Workshop** | Library, SRD pickers, roster import, manual editors, export | Draft realms/adventures/characters/maps from seeds |
| **VTT** | Sheets, tokens, grid, dice, player view, local session sync | Optional blurbs or notes from prompts |

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — manual path first, AI optional
<button onClick={openBlankSheet}>New character sheet</button>
<button onClick={importMarkdown}>Import .md</button>
<button onClick={generateWithAi}>Generate with AI (optional)</button>

// ❌ BAD — no way to proceed without AI
if (!hasApiKey) return <p>Add API keys to use the Virtual Table.</p>
```

When choosing scope, ask: *Can a DM prep and run a session using only manual tools and saved assets?* If not, fix that before adding more AI.

Related principles: `workshop-library` (data tiers) and `scale-portability` (build small, port to larger environments without rewrites).
